training-agents-into-weights-4 : Part
training-agents-into-weights-4 = referring (cons "> My paper which is initial context for all our work, is almost your context window limit. I've" (cons "> graduated from Claude & need to post-train into weights rather than supply inference time context." (cons "> […] It'll be cracked if I can post train agents I know all the irrationalities/biases which damage" (cons "> capacity to work effectively on my work and frankly my mathematical results are beyond what's" (cons "> published to date - shouldn't repeat developing understanding in each session, instead get" (cons "> everything I consider basic context into weights" (cons "" nil))))))) (cons "Avik, 2026-11-15 (evening, Pacific), in conversation with Claude, on why he would train agents into weights rather than supply context at inference:" (cons "" (cons "> My paper which is initial context for all our work, is almost your context window limit. I've" (cons "> graduated from Claude & need to post-train into weights rather than supply inference time context." (cons "> […] It'll be cracked if I can post train agents I know all the irrationalities/biases which damage" (cons "> capacity to work effectively on my work and frankly my mathematical results are beyond what's" (cons "> published to date - shouldn't repeat developing understanding in each session, instead get" (cons "> everything I consider basic context into weights" nil))))))))
training-agents-into-weights-5 : Part
training-agents-into-weights-5 = referring (cons "> Also with hyperactivity I'd love to leave behind Claude/chatgpt UIs and build everything directly" (cons "> exactly the way a rational intelligence builds […] ie owning my info space end-to-end is essential" (cons "" nil))) (cons "Avik, 2026-11-15 (evening, Pacific), in conversation with Claude, on why he would train agents into weights rather than supply context at inference:" (cons "" (cons "> Also with hyperactivity I'd love to leave behind Claude/chatgpt UIs and build everything directly" (cons "> exactly the way a rational intelligence builds […] ie owning my info space end-to-end is essential" nil))))
